# Story 86: Loading & Running Pipelines (50s)
# Hook: Define a pipeline in a file, load it, run it -- ##pipe drives the whole lifecycle.
# Duration: 50s
# Source: story-086-loading-running-pipelines.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 8

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Define a pipeline in a file, load it, run it -- ##pipe drives the whole lifecycle.

[00:03.0 --> 00:08.0]
Start rysh. Pipelines live as files under .rysh/pipelines in your project.

[00:08.0 --> 00:14.0]
Double-Escape into rysh mode. ##pipe help lists everything the pipeline command can do.

[00:14.0 --> 00:22.0]
##pipe load build.pipeline reads the file from .rysh/pipelines and registers it in this tab.

[00:22.0 --> 00:28.0]
##pipe list shows what's loaded; ##pipe show prints a pipeline's steps and details.

[00:28.0 --> 00:38.0]
##pipe run executes it -- defaulting to the first loaded pipeline when you omit the name.

[00:38.0 --> 00:45.0]
##pipe status reports execution progress phase by phase.

[00:45.0 --> 00:50.0]
And ##pipe clear wipes the pipeline output when you're done. Load, run, status, clear -- the full loop.

